 ## Overview
-Feature-Guided Diffusion for Inverse Rendering (FIDE) is a fully black-box framework for solving non-differentiable inverse rendering problems by combining a diffusion-based inverse prediction model with Covariance Matrix Adaptation Evolution Strategy (CMA-ES) [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of finding parameters $\mathbf{x}$ that produce a target image $\mathbf{y}^*$ without requiring gradients from the renderer, treating the rendering function $f$ as an opaque black box [S1, unofficial]. Unlike scalar-loss baselines like DiBO or DiffBBO, FIDE conditions the proposal distribution on dense visual features extracted from the target image, avoiding the information bottleneck of scalar loss values and mitigating mode averaging in ill-posed inverse problems [S1, unofficial].
+Feature-Guided Diffusion for Inverse Rendering (FIDE) is a fully black-box optimization framework that solves non-differentiable inverse rendering problems by combining a diffusion-based inverse predictor with a Covariance Matrix Adaptation Evolution Strategy (CMA-ES) [S1, unofficial]. Unlike scalar-loss baselines like [Optimization Baselines](6675-optimization-baselines.md) or Bayesian optimization methods such as DiBO, FIDE extracts dense visual features from the target image to guide candidate proposal, thereby avoiding the information bottleneck of single-number loss values and the mode-averaging pitfalls of direct regression [S1, unofficial]. It is specifically designed to handle the multi-modal ambiguity inherent in inverse graphics, where multiple parameter sets can produce identical images, by approximating the inverse function as a multi-modal conditional distribution [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-FIDE operates within the standard inverse rendering loop defined by [Optimization Loops and Training Procedures](5622-optimization-loops-and-training-procedures.md), minimizing a photometric loss $\mathcal{L}$ between rendered color $\hat{C}(\mathbf{r})$ and ground-truth $C(\mathbf{r})$ [G]. The core mechanism involves maintaining a search distribution $\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\mu}, \boldsymbol{\Sigma})$ over the parameter space $\mathbb{R}^d$, where $\boldsymbol{\mu}$ is the mean and $\boldsymbol{\Sigma}$ is the anisotropic covariance matrix capturing correlations between parameters [S1, unofficial].
-
-The method alternates between an inverse prediction step (using a diffusion model conditioned on image features) and an evolution step (using CMA-ES) to solve non-differentiable inverse problems [S1, unofficial].
+FIDE operates within the standard inverse rendering loop defined by [Optimization Loops and Training Procedures](5622-optimization-loops-and-training-procedures.md), minimizing a photometric loss $\mathcal{L}$ between rendered color $\hat{C}(\mathbf{r})$ and ground-truth $C(\mathbf{r})$ [G]. The core mechanism alternates between an inverse prediction step using a diffusion model conditioned on image features and an evolution step using CMA-ES to refine the search space [S1, unofficial].
 
